    think:{quote:"Jack lifts his knife high above a piglet trapped in the vines, but for a long moment he cannot make himself bring it down.", question:"Jack cannot kill the piglet in this chapter. Why do you think this is so hard for him?", options:["Because he is afraid of the small piglet","Because killing is very different from the rules he has always followed at home","Because Ralph orders him to stop"], answer:1, note:"Jack has grown up with strict rules against hurting living things; the shock of really killing stops his hand, at least for now."},
